    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d977">

                <pb facs="0957" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg699"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-09T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 9, 1915, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>922. Your 1437, January 8. Department is advising commercial bodies and telegraph
                    companies to use, as far as possible, plain English words in cable messages.</p>
                <p>Can you arrange to have the senders of stopped messages immediately informed so
                    that there may be as little financial loss as possible?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
